                    </div>

                    <!-- 📚 Part 1: What are Generics? (Super Simple) -->
                    <section class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">
                        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg" style="border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden;">
                            <div class="card-header" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4facfe 0%, #00f2fe 100%); color: white; border: none;">
                                <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-1 me-2"></i>Part 1: What are Generics? (The Easy Way)</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body p-4">
                                <div class="alert alert-info">
                                    <i class="fas fa-question-circle me-2"></i>
                                    <strong>In Simple Words:</strong> Generics let you write code that works with <strong>any type</strong> of data,
                                    but still keeps everything <strong>type-safe</strong> (no mistakes!).
                                </div>

                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-box text-primary me-2"></i>📦 The Box Analogy</h5>
                                                <p>Think of a <strong>generic class</strong> as a box:</p>
                                                <ul>
                                                    <li>📦 The <strong>box</strong> is the same shape (the class)</li>
                                                    <li>📦 You can put <strong>books</strong> in it (strings)</li>
                                                    <li>📦 You can put <strong>toys</strong> in it (integers)</li>
                                                    <li>📦 You can put <strong>clothes</strong> in it (custom objects)</li>
                                                    <li>📦 The box <strong>remembers</strong> what's inside!</li>
                                                </ul>
                                                <div class="alert alert-success mt-2">
                                                    <i class="fas fa-check-circle me-2"></i>
                                                    <strong>That's Generics:</strong> One box, many types!
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-code text-primary me-2"></i>💻 Code Time!</h5>
                                                <p><strong>Generic Class:</strong></p>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="comment">// 📦 A Box that can hold ANY type</span>
<span class="keyword">public</span> <span class="keyword">class</span> <span class="class">Box</span>&lt;T&gt;  <span class="comment">// T = Type placeholder</span>
{
    <span class="keyword">private</span> T item;  <span class="comment">// Can be any type!</span>
    
    <span class="keyword">public</span> <span class="keyword">void</span> <span class="function">Store</span>(T value) => item = value;
    <span class="keyword">public</span> T <span class="function">Retrieve</span>() => item;
}</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                                <p><strong>Using the Box:</strong></p>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="comment">// Box for numbers</span>
<span class="class">Box</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">int</span>&gt; intBox = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">Box</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">int</span>&gt;();
intBox.<span class="function">Store</span>(<span class="number">42</span>);
<span class="keyword">int</span> value = intBox.<span class="function">Retrieve</span>();  <span class="comment">// Safe! No casting!</span>

<span class="comment">// Box for text</span>
<span class="class">Box</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>&gt; strBox = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">Box</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>&gt;();
strBox.<span class="function">Store</span>(<span class="string">"Hello!"</span>);</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                                <div class="alert alert-warning mt-2">
                                                    <i class="fas fa-star me-2"></i>
                                                    <strong>🎉 Same class, different types!</strong>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="card bg-success text-white mt-3">
                                    <div class="card-body">
                                        <i class="fas fa-laugh-beam me-2"></i>
                                        <strong>😂 Fun Joke:</strong> Why did the generic class break up with the specific type?
                                        Because it wanted to see other types! (Okay, I'll stop 😅)
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- 🧩 Part 2: Generic Classes - The Reusable Container -->
                    <section class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">
                        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg" style="border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden;">
                            <div class="card-header" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43e97b 0%, #38f9d7 100%); color: white; border: none;">
                                <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-2 me-2"></i>Part 2: Generic Classes - The Reusable Container</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body p-4">
                                <p class="fs-5">A <strong>generic class</strong> uses a placeholder type (like <code>T</code>) that you fill in later.</p>

                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-code text-primary me-2"></i>📝 Generic Class Example</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="comment">// 📦 A generic storage class</span>
<span class="keyword">public</span> <span class="keyword">class</span> <span class="class">Storage</span>&lt;T&gt;
{
    <span class="keyword">private</span> <span class="class">List</span>&lt;T&gt; items = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">List</span>&lt;T&gt;();
    
    <span class="keyword">public</span> <span class="keyword">void</span> <span class="function">Add</span>(T item) => items.<span class="function">Add</span>(item);
    <span class="keyword">public</span> T <span class="function">Get</span>(<span class="keyword">int</span> index) => items[index];
    <span class="keyword">public</span> <span class="keyword">int</span> Count => items.Count;
}</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-play text-success me-2"></i>🎯 Using It</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="comment">// Storage for numbers</span>
<span class="class">Storage</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">int</span>&gt; numStore = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">Storage</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">int</span>&gt;();
numStore.<span class="function">Add</span>(<span class="number">5</span>);
numStore.<span class="function">Add</span>(<span class="number">10</span>);

<span class="comment">// Storage for names</span>
<span class="class">Storage</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>&gt; nameStore = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">Storage</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>&gt;();
nameStore.<span class="function">Add</span>(<span class="string">"Alice"</span>);
nameStore.<span class="function">Add</span>(<span class="string">"Bob"</span>);</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                                <p><span class="badge bg-success">✅</span> One class, many types!</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                                    <i class="fas fa-check-circle me-2"></i>
                                    <strong>Why Use Generic Classes?</strong>
                                    <ul class="mb-0">
                                        <li>✅ <strong>Reusable</strong> - Write once, use with any type</li>
                                        <li>✅ <strong>Type-Safe</strong> - No casting errors</li>
                                        <li>✅ <strong>Clean</strong> - No messy <code>object</code> code</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- 🛠️ Part 3: Generic Methods -->
                    <section class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">
                        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg" style="border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden;">
                            <div class="card-header" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f093fb 0%, #f5576c 100%); color: white; border: none;">
                                <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-3 me-2"></i>Part 3: Generic Methods - Flexible Functions</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body p-4">
                                <p class="fs-5">A <strong>generic method</strong> can work with different types, even if the class isn't generic!</p>

                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-code text-primary me-2"></i>📝 Generic Method</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="keyword">public</span> <span class="keyword">class</span> <span class="class">Helper</span>
{
    <span class="comment">// 🔄 Swaps any two values</span>
    <span class="keyword">public</span> <span class="keyword">void</span> <span class="function">Swap</span>&lt;T&gt;(<span class="keyword">ref</span> T a, <span class="keyword">ref</span> T b)
    {
        T temp = a;
        a = b;
        b = temp;
    }
    
    <span class="comment">// 📏 Returns the bigger of two</span>
    <span class="keyword">public</span> T <span class="function">Max</span>&lt;T&gt;(T a, T b) <span class="keyword">where</span> T : <span class="class">IComparable</span>&lt;T&gt;
    {
        <span class="keyword">return</span> a.<span class="function">CompareTo</span>(b) > <span class="number">0</span> ? a : b;
    }
}</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-play text-success me-2"></i>🎯 Using It</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="class">Helper</span> helper = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">Helper</span>();

<span class="comment">// Swap integers</span>
<span class="keyword">int</span> x = <span class="number">5</span>, y = <span class="number">10</span>;
helper.<span class="function">Swap</span>(<span class="keyword">ref</span> x, <span class="keyword">ref</span> y);
<span class="comment">// x=10, y=5</span>

<span class="comment">// Swap strings</span>
<span class="keyword">string</span> a = <span class="string">"Hello"</span>, b = <span class="string">"World"</span>;
helper.<span class="function">Swap</span>(<span class="keyword">ref</span> a, <span class="keyword">ref</span> b);

<span class="comment">// Get max</span>
<span class="keyword">int</span> max = helper.<span class="function">Max</span>(<span class="number">5</span>, <span class="number">10</span>);  <span class="comment">// 10</span></code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                                <p><span class="badge bg-success">✅</span> Same method, different types!</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="card bg-warning mt-3">
                                    <div class="card-body">
                                        <i class="fas fa-lightbulb me-2"></i>
                                        <strong>Remember:</strong> The <code>&lt;T&gt;</code> after the method name tells C# "This method uses generics!"
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- 🔒 Part 4: Generic Constraints - Setting Rules -->
                    <section class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">
                        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg" style="border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden;">
                            <div class="card-header" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%); color: white; border: none;">
                                <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-4 me-2"></i>Part 4: Generic Constraints - Setting Rules</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body p-4">
                                <div class="alert alert-info">
                                    <i class="fas fa-rules me-2"></i>
                                    <strong>What are Constraints?</strong> They're <strong>rules</strong> about what types can be used with your generic!
                                </div>

                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-code text-primary me-2"></i>📝 Constraints Examples</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="comment">// 🚫 T must be a class (reference type)</span>
<span class="keyword">public</span> <span class="keyword">class</span> <span class="class">Processor</span>&lt;T&gt; <span class="keyword">where</span> T : <span class="keyword">class</span>
{
    <span class="keyword">public</span> T <span class="function">Process</span>(T item) => item;
}

<span class="comment">// ✅ T must have a default constructor</span>
<span class="keyword">public</span> <span class="keyword">class</span> <span class="class">Creator</span>&lt;T&gt; <span class="keyword">where</span> T : <span class="keyword">new</span>()
{
    <span class="keyword">public</span> T <span class="function">Create</span>() => <span class="keyword">new</span> T();
}

<span class="comment">// 📊 T must be comparable</span>
<span class="keyword">public</span> T <span class="function">Max</span>&lt;T&gt;(T a, T b) <span class="keyword">where</span> T : <span class="class">IComparable</span>&lt;T&gt;
{
    <span class="keyword">return</span> a.<span class="function">CompareTo</span>(b) > <span class="number">0</span> ? a : b;
}</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>✅ Why Constraints?</h5>
                                                <ul>
                                                    <li>✅ <strong>Safety</strong> - Only valid types can be used</li>
                                                    <li>✅ <strong>Features</strong> - Access methods like <code>CompareTo()</code></li>
                                                    <li>✅ <strong>Clarity</strong> - Other developers know what's allowed</li>
                                                </ul>
                                                <div class="alert alert-success mt-2">
                                                    <i class="fas fa-check-circle me-2"></i>
                                                    <strong>Common Constraints:</strong>
                                                    <ul class="mb-0">
                                                        <li><code>where T : class</code> - T must be a class</li>
                                                        <li><code>where T : struct</code> - T must be a struct</li>
                                                        <li><code>where T : new()</code> - T must have a default constructor</li>
                                                        <li><code>where T : SomeClass</code> - T must inherit from SomeClass</li>
                                                    </ul>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- 📦 Part 5: Generic Collections -->
                    <section class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">
                        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg" style="border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden;">
                            <div class="card-header" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43e97b 0%, #38f9d7 100%); color: white; border: none;">
                                <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-5 me-2"></i>Part 5: Generic Collections - The Most Common Generics</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body p-4">
                                <p class="fs-5">C# has <strong>built-in generic collections</strong> that you'll use every day!</p>

                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-list text-primary me-2"></i>📝 List&lt;T&gt; - A Flexible List</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="class">List</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>&gt; names = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">List</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>&gt;();
names.<span class="function">Add</span>(<span class="string">"Alice"</span>);
names.<span class="function">Add</span>(<span class="string">"Bob"</span>);
<span class="keyword">string</span> first = names[<span class="number">0</span>];</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                                <p><span class="badge bg-info">List</span> Like an array that can grow and shrink</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-book text-primary me-2"></i>📝 Dictionary&lt;TKey, TValue&gt;</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="class">Dictionary</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>, <span class="keyword">int</span>&gt; ages = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">Dictionary</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>, <span class="keyword">int</span>&gt;();
ages.<span class="function">Add</span>(<span class="string">"Alice"</span>, <span class="number">25</span>);
ages.<span class="function">Add</span>(<span class="string">"Bob"</span>, <span class="number">30</span>);
<span class="keyword">int</span> age = ages[<span class="string">"Alice"</span>];  <span class="comment">// 25</span></code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                                <p><span class="badge bg-info">Dictionary</span> Key-Value pairs (like a real dictionary)</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="row mt-3">
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-code text-primary me-2"></i>Other Useful Collections</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="comment">// 🚶 Queue - First In, First Out</span>
<span class="class">Queue</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>&gt; line = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">Queue</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>&gt;();
line.<span class="function">Enqueue</span>(<span class="string">"Person1"</span>);
line.<span class="function">Enqueue</span>(<span class="string">"Person2"</span>);
<span class="keyword">string</span> next = line.<span class="function">Dequeue</span>();  <span class="comment">// "Person1"</span>

<span class="comment">// 📚 Stack - Last In, First Out</span>
<span class="class">Stack</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>&gt; stack = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">Stack</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">string</span>&gt;();
stack.<span class="function">Push</span>(<span class="string">"First"</span>);
stack.<span class="function">Push</span>(<span class="string">"Second"</span>);
<span class="keyword">string</span> last = stack.<span class="function">Pop</span>();  <span class="comment">// "Second"</span></code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>✅ Benefits of Generic Collections</h5>
                                                <ul>
                                                    <li>✅ <strong>Type-Safe</strong> - No casting needed</li>
                                                    <li>✅ <strong>Fast</strong> - No boxing/unboxing</li>
                                                    <li>✅ <strong>Clean</strong> - Easy to read and use</li>
                                                    <li>✅ <strong>Powerful</strong> - Built-in methods (Sort, Find, etc.)</li>
                                                </ul>
                                                <div class="alert alert-success mt-2">
